<title>USA: Martin Marietta increases board size.</title>
<headline>Martin Marietta increases board size.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Martin Marietta Materials Inc said Monday it has elected two new members to its board of directors, increasing the size of the panel to nine members.</p>
<p>William McDonald, president and chief executive of Sprint Corp's MidAtlantic Telecom unit of Raleigh, and Richard Vinroot, a partner in the Charlotte law firm of Robinson, Bradshaw and Hinson, were named to the board.</p>
<p>Vinroot was mayor of Charlotte from 1991 through 1995.</p>
